after a couple of days more with all the components that i've ordered on aliex. i've come to the realization that the designer, a guy named 'foostan', decided that for the v.3 of the contraption that is a split keyboard, he was not only gonna upgrade the key leds with decent ones (v.2 have, and i'm not kidding, the very worst piece of leds ever invented), and, not only that, but to flip vertically the led placement and the switch harness, so now you can enjoy your leds glowing AT THE BOTTOM SIDE OF THE KEYCAP insted of the top side, i suspect this was done so you can place transparent keycaps and still enjoy the lighting effects, but FOR PEOPLE LIKE ME WHOSE KEYCAPS HAVE THE LETTERS ENGRAVED AT THE TOP SIDE, LIKE ALL THE FUCKING KEYCAPS IN THE WORLD, now you have a keyboard without lighting, THANK YOU VERY MUCH, and since i'm not gonna throw away my razer blackwidow ultimate keycaps, i'm sentenced to utilize the v.2 with it's gloriously bad leds

so after assembling the v.2 yet again, and fix another two other corrupt leds, undone everything to it's prior state and went to fix the custom firmware

i've managed to gather bits and pieces of the last efforts, and after the remainder of the afternoon, managed to bring AGAIN the corne to a semi-state of completeness, sans the lighting on the slave side and the reactive semiotic standard icons on the master side, which was where it left the project in the previous run

my strategy now is to start anew, but focusing on solving this two issues only, in isolation, it would be easier to integrate everything else, since the keymaps, graphics and all are just cosmetics
